'' --diagnostics-file: a TOOLCHAIN failure is a diagnostic too, and still exits with the
'' toolchain's code.
''
'' 'tiko: clang not found' used to be printed straight to stderr, outside the engine, so
'' an editor reading the file saw a failed build with no errors in it. It is TKO0111 now,
'' location-less -- and the exit code is still 3, not the 1 that 'the engine holds an
'' error' would have produced: ToolFail_ counts it as the toolchain's.
''
'' TKO_CLANG names a file that cannot exist, so this needs no clang, no linker and no
'' runtime on the machine running it (see toolchain-exit.test).
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_CLANG=tests/driver/src/no-such-clang.exe
'' ARGS: -o build/.diagfile-tool.exe --diagnostics-file build/.diagfile-tool.tsv tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 3
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0111: no usable toolchain: clang not found
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-tool.tsv :: \nerror\tTKO0111\t\t0\t0\t0\t0\tno usable toolchain: clang not found
'' ...and the one warning is TKO0124, said before the front end ran: no LLVM at all.
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-tool.tsv :: \nwarning\tTKO0124\t
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-tool.tsv :: \nend\t1\t1\t3\n
